WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.134 --> 00:00:01.240
(child yelling)

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.137
- It changes you.

00:00:02.137 --> 00:00:04.331
- [Ned] Don't you punch my weiner!

00:00:04.331 --> 00:00:06.539
(children yelling)

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.232
- I am so overwhelmed.

00:00:08.232 --> 00:00:09.363
(laughing)

00:00:09.363 --> 00:00:12.363
(lively jazz music)

00:00:24.237 --> 00:00:26.583
We're here, we're doing it,
today we're raising kids!

00:00:26.583 --> 00:00:29.536
- So I'm gonna be raising
someone else's child for a day.

00:00:29.536 --> 00:00:30.550
- Oh, good luck.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:31.607
(laughing)
- I don't know what to think.

00:00:31.607 --> 00:00:33.031
- You're not qualified.

00:00:33.031 --> 00:00:33.867
(laughs)

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.252
- So what was I like as a toddler?

00:00:35.252 --> 00:00:36.699
- Complete pain in the ass.

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:38.535
- [Eugene's Dad] You were
daydreaming every day.

00:00:38.535 --> 00:00:39.920
- When you were two and you were three,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.663
you were really strong-willed.

00:00:41.663 --> 00:00:43.960
- Me and my wife are pretty
close to having children.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.331
- I'm still not so good
at taking care of myself.

00:00:46.331 --> 00:00:48.725
- I'm not the most fond of babies.

00:00:48.725 --> 00:00:51.221
- It'll be fun, I'm a boy,
I get along with boys.

00:00:51.221 --> 00:00:52.054
I mean look at all these toys.

00:00:52.054 --> 00:00:53.204
We're gonna have a great time.

00:00:53.204 --> 00:00:55.954
(crying)
- Uh-oh.

00:00:57.395 --> 00:00:58.298
- It's tiring.

00:00:58.298 --> 00:00:59.185
- You're losing sleep.

00:00:59.185 --> 00:01:00.264
- Every day is new.

00:01:00.264 --> 00:01:02.625
- It's like having a tornado for a pet.

00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:04.782
- There he goes.
- I have to go for that one.

00:01:04.782 --> 00:01:06.398
- It's like taking care
of your drunk friend.

00:01:06.398 --> 00:01:10.620
- My name is David, I have
a 14-month-old son Isadore.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.453
- You're a rockst-- ow!

00:01:11.453 --> 00:01:15.385
- Anything that he is not
supposed to get, he wants.

00:01:15.385 --> 00:01:17.019
- Hey, what did you just find on this?

00:01:17.019 --> 00:01:18.391
Yeah, not good, dude.

00:01:18.391 --> 00:01:20.938
Dominik is 22 months, just turned it.

00:01:20.938 --> 00:01:22.233
- Oh it's in his, it's in his mouth.

00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:23.808
(laughing)

00:01:23.808 --> 00:01:26.673
Just really going at it,
just really chewing it.

00:01:26.673 --> 00:01:27.810
- This is a two-year-old.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.036
- Woah, woah, woah, hey, hey!

00:01:29.036 --> 00:01:30.352
- Good catch!

00:01:30.352 --> 00:01:31.385
Better dad than me.

00:01:31.385 --> 00:01:35.062
So this is Oskar, and then
I have a 7-week-old at home.

00:01:35.062 --> 00:01:36.675
He did say at one point
he wanted to throw him

00:01:36.675 --> 00:01:38.293
in the trash can.

00:01:38.293 --> 00:01:39.947
(screaming, crying)

00:01:39.947 --> 00:01:41.281
- Dex, don't take a book
from a baby sweetheart,

00:01:41.281 --> 00:01:42.628
for what I consider to be obvious reasons.

00:01:42.628 --> 00:01:43.879
(yells)

00:01:43.879 --> 00:01:44.712
- So this is your life?

00:01:44.712 --> 00:01:46.927
- This is Odysseus,
he's one, Ajax is four,

00:01:46.927 --> 00:01:49.548
and Rex is six, six and a half.

00:01:49.548 --> 00:01:50.565
- What's it like to be a dad?

00:01:50.565 --> 00:01:52.608
- It's constantly--
(baby screams)

00:01:52.608 --> 00:01:53.624
Constant chaos.

00:01:53.624 --> 00:01:56.613
- When you have a kid,
you sign up for stress.

00:01:56.613 --> 00:01:58.377
- As soon as they get to
like, 10 months, that's

00:01:58.377 --> 00:02:01.350
when they start crawling,
and that's crazy town.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.448
- He's like a wild little beast.

00:02:03.448 --> 00:02:04.673
(children yelling)

00:02:04.673 --> 00:02:05.955
- Yeah.

00:02:05.955 --> 00:02:07.533
- I couldn't get anything
done with these three.

00:02:07.533 --> 00:02:08.480
- You don't get anything done!

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.529
I mean you go to sleep at 1:30
or 2:00, you get up at 5:30.

00:02:11.529 --> 00:02:12.389
You've seen me, you know me.

00:02:12.389 --> 00:02:13.557
How do I get, I don't know?

00:02:13.557 --> 00:02:16.215
- So I'm gonna, I guess
sort of reverse Asian this

00:02:16.215 --> 00:02:18.103
and be the adoptive father?

00:02:18.103 --> 00:02:19.660
- Hello Oskar, I'm Ned.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.411
- So I'm your dad now.

00:02:21.411 --> 00:02:23.528
- I'll be hanging out with you today.

00:02:23.528 --> 00:02:24.697
Does that sound like a good time?

00:02:24.697 --> 00:02:25.530
- Uh-uh.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:26.433
- No.

00:02:26.433 --> 00:02:27.786
- You're not gonna like,
throw up on me, are ya?

00:02:27.786 --> 00:02:30.597
- Dominik, come here!
- Dom, wait, Dom, come back.

00:02:30.597 --> 00:02:33.266
- Dragging the baby was never
in any of my parenting books.

00:02:33.266 --> 00:02:36.503
- (chuckling) He's tripped six
times in the last ten steps.

00:02:36.503 --> 00:02:37.636
(humming)

00:02:37.636 --> 00:02:39.704
- Do you think Ned's boring?

00:02:39.704 --> 00:02:41.045
(laughing)

00:02:41.045 --> 00:02:42.330
- (laughing) There he goes again!

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.619
- Do children often try to just get away?

00:02:44.619 --> 00:02:46.419
- That one does, yeah.

00:02:46.419 --> 00:02:47.771
(laughing)

00:02:47.771 --> 00:02:50.771
- Now why doesn't Ned try to tickle?

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.437
(laughing)

00:02:53.437 --> 00:02:54.300
- Fetch!

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.028
- Alright, well, it looks like you have

00:02:56.028 --> 00:02:57.413
your work cut out for you, Ned.

00:02:57.413 --> 00:03:00.580
- Is it rude for me to say I want out?

00:03:02.036 --> 00:03:03.448
- Do you think I'm gonna do well?

00:03:03.448 --> 00:03:04.799
- Uhh, wouldn't say.

00:03:04.799 --> 00:03:06.246
(laughs)

00:03:06.246 --> 00:03:07.482
- It's daddy time!

00:03:07.482 --> 00:03:09.201
My main goal today is just to make sure

00:03:09.201 --> 00:03:10.863
that the kid doesn't die.

00:03:10.863 --> 00:03:12.142
- Make sure nobody chokes to death.

00:03:12.142 --> 00:03:14.516
I've never choked to
death, so I'm an expert.

00:03:14.516 --> 00:03:15.708
- My strengths today are

00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:18.416
I've got a lot of energy, I'm ready to go,

00:03:18.416 --> 00:03:22.430
and my weaknesses are
I don't know anything.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:23.263
- Hello!

00:03:23.263 --> 00:03:24.346
- I'll knock.

00:03:26.159 --> 00:03:27.371
- Hey!
- Hello!

00:03:27.371 --> 00:03:28.294
- Can you say hi to Ned?

00:03:28.294 --> 00:03:29.127
- Hi, Ned.

00:03:29.127 --> 00:03:31.717
- This is your domain,
you can be daddy now.

00:03:31.717 --> 00:03:32.587
- I am daddy.

00:03:32.587 --> 00:03:35.175
- You basically just keep him alive.

00:03:35.175 --> 00:03:37.187
- He needs a change, this
is what he wore to sleep.

00:03:37.187 --> 00:03:39.268
- Hopefully I don't (bleep) this up.

00:03:39.268 --> 00:03:42.908
- He does repeat things, so watch out.

00:03:42.908 --> 00:03:43.741
- Okay.

00:03:43.741 --> 00:03:44.574
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

00:03:44.574 --> 00:03:46.403
- You're a dad to me, I
will be in the other room.

00:03:46.403 --> 00:03:47.518
Boys, entertain him!

00:03:47.518 --> 00:03:52.163
- I will, um, figure out
what to do with you, Dom.

00:03:52.163 --> 00:03:53.407
- Where's daddy?

00:03:53.407 --> 00:03:54.568
- Oh, see, already hates me.

00:03:54.568 --> 00:03:56.108
Already doesn't wanna stay with me.

00:03:56.108 --> 00:03:57.743
Off to a great start.

00:03:57.743 --> 00:03:59.484
Oh, I should take care
of this kid, alright,

00:03:59.484 --> 00:04:00.317
(bleep) ouch.

00:04:00.317 --> 00:04:01.963
Oh, (bleep)!

00:04:01.963 --> 00:04:03.407
Oh my god I keep saying it!

00:04:03.407 --> 00:04:05.168
(laughing)

00:04:05.168 --> 00:04:06.450
Okay, I'm not gonna, whoo!

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.927
- I was the youngest of three boys,

00:04:08.927 --> 00:04:10.773
but I've never dealt with the chaos

00:04:10.773 --> 00:04:13.657
that was my own childhood dynamic.

00:04:13.657 --> 00:04:14.825
- Alright, I'm your dad today.

00:04:14.825 --> 00:04:17.827
Could we put down the screen, Ajax?

00:04:17.827 --> 00:04:20.576
- He still isn't of the age
where you can reason with him.

00:04:20.576 --> 00:04:21.409
- Dom, where'd you go?

00:04:21.409 --> 00:04:23.022
- Hey, Ajax, Ajax!

00:04:23.022 --> 00:04:23.855
- Dom!

00:04:23.855 --> 00:04:26.472
- Your dad's, I'm your dad
now, and screen time's over,

00:04:26.472 --> 00:04:27.575
I don't know where you're going.

00:04:27.575 --> 00:04:29.764
- Okay lets, do you
take your own shirt off?

00:04:29.764 --> 00:04:31.665
Or, do you want me to help you or what?

00:04:31.665 --> 00:04:33.119
- Book.

00:04:33.119 --> 00:04:33.952
- Butts?

00:04:33.952 --> 00:04:34.875
- Dom, wait for me.

00:04:34.875 --> 00:04:36.688
Dom, Dom, Dom.

00:04:36.688 --> 00:04:38.159
- Ajax, where are you at?

00:04:38.159 --> 00:04:40.817
Ajax, we don't need the cupcake tin.

00:04:40.817 --> 00:04:42.299
What, here, why are you opening this?

00:04:42.299 --> 00:04:44.359
- Underwear goes off, okay.

00:04:44.359 --> 00:04:45.696
And now we got Star Wars.

00:04:45.696 --> 00:04:48.031
Oh, can't run around naked!

00:04:48.031 --> 00:04:49.614
- Hit this, not me.

00:04:50.764 --> 00:04:51.616
No, no, not me!

00:04:51.616 --> 00:04:52.449
(clattering)

00:04:52.449 --> 00:04:54.340
- I'm gonna eat.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.981
- You okay over there Ajax?

00:04:55.981 --> 00:04:56.814
- Follow me.

00:04:56.814 --> 00:04:57.652
(clicks tongue)

00:04:57.652 --> 00:05:00.017
Oh wait, no, that's what you do to a dog.

00:05:00.017 --> 00:05:01.940
- [Ari] Alright, baby's up,
let's go meet that baby.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:02.979
- The baby's awake?

00:05:02.979 --> 00:05:04.626
It's time to add another child to this

00:05:04.626 --> 00:05:07.347
because I'm in too much control!

00:05:07.347 --> 00:05:10.041
I need to go take care of your brother.

00:05:10.041 --> 00:05:13.210
And then, can you guys, do you guys wanna

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.750
Should we give them a screen for a minute?

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.721
What do you do?

00:05:16.721 --> 00:05:19.289
You got five minutes of
screen time, how's that sound?

00:05:19.289 --> 00:05:20.723
- Great!

00:05:20.723 --> 00:05:23.166
- Try not to kill each
other while I'm gone.

00:05:23.166 --> 00:05:24.760
- We're gonna kill each other?

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:25.830
- Yeah, don't.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.108
- Why?

00:05:27.108 --> 00:05:29.898
- I feel like that's a
pretty obvious reason.

00:05:29.898 --> 00:05:31.653
Hey, who's this?

00:05:31.653 --> 00:05:33.117
It's a stranger!

00:05:33.117 --> 00:05:35.328
Good morning, Otis!

00:05:35.328 --> 00:05:36.197
What are you wearing?

00:05:36.197 --> 00:05:37.578
You are too adorable.

00:05:37.578 --> 00:05:40.038
He's killing it with those blue squares.

00:05:40.038 --> 00:05:42.819
- When you have kids, your
whole life changes dramatically,

00:05:42.819 --> 00:05:44.141
especially the first one.

00:05:44.141 --> 00:05:45.747
- Oh, Otis, you do not smell the best.

00:05:45.747 --> 00:05:48.889
- I've got my day job, so a
lot of days I'm just not home.

00:05:48.889 --> 00:05:50.657
- Three, two, one, up we go!

00:05:50.657 --> 00:05:51.840
- So those nights where I am home

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.509
were nights where she works,
then the sort of understanding

00:05:53.509 --> 00:05:55.727
is I will try to do everything then.

00:05:55.727 --> 00:05:57.084
- Hi boys, how you doing?

00:05:57.084 --> 00:05:59.273
I got a third boy for ya.

00:05:59.273 --> 00:06:00.106
Oh no?

00:06:00.106 --> 00:06:02.236
What do you mean, oh no?

00:06:02.236 --> 00:06:03.254
He's trouble?

00:06:03.254 --> 00:06:05.167
(baby cooing)

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:07.363
- I mean I have all these
advantages and it's hard as hell.

00:06:07.363 --> 00:06:08.613
I've got a wife who's a great partner,

00:06:08.613 --> 00:06:10.162
I've got a good job, my kids are healthy,

00:06:10.162 --> 00:06:11.501
and it's super, super, super hard.

00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:12.531
- Look at him dance!

00:06:12.531 --> 00:06:13.784
Hey guys, look at him dance!

00:06:13.784 --> 00:06:14.617
(chuckles)

00:06:14.617 --> 00:06:16.797
- Given that, how dare I not at least

00:06:16.797 --> 00:06:18.720
do my best at this?

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:19.553
- Ajax--

00:06:19.553 --> 00:06:22.303
(dramatic music)

00:06:23.563 --> 00:06:24.563
- Hey, hey, hey guys!

00:06:24.563 --> 00:06:27.367
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:29.784
Both of you, hey, guys, guys!

00:06:30.953 --> 00:06:32.484
Hey, Rex!

00:06:32.484 --> 00:06:33.653
Can you guys both apologize to each other

00:06:33.653 --> 00:06:35.505
for hitting each other?

00:06:35.505 --> 00:06:36.726
You can, you can.

00:06:36.726 --> 00:06:38.212
- Not everything's a teachable moment,

00:06:38.212 --> 00:06:39.045
that's the other thing.

00:06:39.045 --> 00:06:41.665
And that's taken me three kids
and six years to figure out.

00:06:41.665 --> 00:06:42.876
- Are we chill?

00:06:42.876 --> 00:06:44.959
Hey, give me that screen.

00:06:45.842 --> 00:06:47.066
What are you doing--

00:06:47.066 --> 00:06:48.617
(blowing raspberry)

00:06:48.617 --> 00:06:49.750
- How do I get him to like me?

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:52.939
- [David] The way you would
want to get anyone to like you.

00:06:52.939 --> 00:06:54.501
- I'm still trying to figure that out.

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:56.430
- Dom, do you wanna play with chalk?

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.429
Okay, I think he understood what I said.

00:06:58.429 --> 00:07:00.257
- He's happy unless he cries, right?

00:07:00.257 --> 00:07:03.257
- [David] I mean, he can get stoked.

00:07:04.177 --> 00:07:05.806
- Yeah, throw things!

00:07:05.806 --> 00:07:07.456
- We're gonna make something to eat.

00:07:07.456 --> 00:07:08.808
I don't even know where to start.

00:07:08.808 --> 00:07:09.780
(baby yells)

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.249
Yeah!

00:07:11.249 --> 00:07:12.935
Man I really regret taking
you out of the seat.

00:07:12.935 --> 00:07:15.482
- [Ned] You're doing
a great job unpacking.

00:07:15.482 --> 00:07:16.315
Uh-oh.

00:07:16.315 --> 00:07:17.235
- Yeah!

00:07:17.235 --> 00:07:18.901
(bleep) that guy--Oh, man.

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:20.927
I'm sorry, you didn't hear that.

00:07:20.927 --> 00:07:21.882
- Oh, man!

00:07:21.882 --> 00:07:23.715
- I know, oh man, see,

00:07:24.772 --> 00:07:26.769
he retained the second
part of that sentence.

00:07:26.769 --> 00:07:28.795
- Hey Izzy, you wanna go fast?

00:07:28.795 --> 00:07:29.678
You wanna go whee?

00:07:29.678 --> 00:07:30.511
Whee!

00:07:32.938 --> 00:07:34.406
Little bit of a whiplash,
there, you're good, though.

00:07:34.406 --> 00:07:36.631
(making eating noises)

00:07:36.631 --> 00:07:39.180
(baby talking)
(gasp)

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.349
- Normally I think quiet babies are not

00:07:40.349 --> 00:07:42.673
that cute, but this one's really cute.

00:07:42.673 --> 00:07:43.552
Congratulations!

00:07:43.552 --> 00:07:45.669
- I think he's getting the hang of it.

00:07:45.669 --> 00:07:46.502
- Whee!

00:07:47.417 --> 00:07:50.671
- Please Dom, have mercy! Ahh, no!

00:07:50.671 --> 00:07:51.989
(laughs)

00:07:51.989 --> 00:07:53.832
- And now the ultimate
challenge of the dad,

00:07:53.832 --> 00:07:56.127
using an oven while holding a baby.

00:07:56.127 --> 00:07:58.116
(making noises, laughing)

00:07:58.116 --> 00:07:59.697
- Just everything's a game.

00:07:59.697 --> 00:08:00.530
Ahh!

00:08:01.683 --> 00:08:03.924
- Get a little eyeshadow.

00:08:03.924 --> 00:08:05.615
Oh no, no, don't actually do it, though.

00:08:05.615 --> 00:08:06.448
- No, no, no, no

00:08:06.448 --> 00:08:08.565
- They have a tendency to
put everything in his mouth.

00:08:08.565 --> 00:08:10.352
- [Zach] No, no, no, no.

00:08:10.352 --> 00:08:11.570
- Are kids allowed to eat chalk?

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:12.403
Probably not, okay.

00:08:12.403 --> 00:08:13.236
Let's take that off.

00:08:13.236 --> 00:08:15.441
Oh yeah, lets spit that
out, spit that out.

00:08:15.441 --> 00:08:16.274
- We can't just eat flour.

00:08:16.274 --> 00:08:17.107
- We're not!

00:08:17.107 --> 00:08:18.204
- You were!

00:08:18.204 --> 00:08:19.285
- Now he's eating a pencil.

00:08:19.285 --> 00:08:20.990
- So we're almost
halfway through this day,

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:24.010
and Oskar and I still
aren't really connecting.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:26.276
Do you wanna walk around
the kitchen with me?

00:08:26.276 --> 00:08:28.443
(singing)

00:08:29.336 --> 00:08:30.958
So what was I like as a child?

00:08:30.958 --> 00:08:34.524
- You weren't verbal at
all in the beginning.

00:08:34.524 --> 00:08:36.319
(grunting)

00:08:36.319 --> 00:08:37.330
- Do you know how to play the guitar?

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:40.142
(strums guitar, sings)

00:08:40.142 --> 00:08:41.565
What more do you want?

00:08:41.565 --> 00:08:43.308
How do you know when
you're ready to have kids?

00:08:43.308 --> 00:08:44.223
- You're never ready.

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:46.022
- Gotta use your feet!

00:08:46.022 --> 00:08:46.861
Alright.

00:08:46.861 --> 00:08:48.668
- It tests the relationship like no other.

00:08:48.668 --> 00:08:50.250
- I think my wife and I are pretty good

